# The BoringSSL the `boringssl` provider package is built from
# (HTTP-CLIENT-PACKAGE-MILESTONE-1.md, "The provider"). A Tcl dict, read by
# tools/http-package.tcl.
#
# The revision is the one boring-sys 5.4.0 vendors (its deps/boringssl at
# cloudflare/boring 309bf35b), upstream's release tag 0.20261020.0, the
# HTTP stack census's provider (audit/http-stack/boringssl/PIN). It is
# built from upstream, unpatched and unprefixed (the `boring` crate cannot
# consume a prefixed build: HTTP-SHIPPING-CENSUS.md's B7), in one archive of
# its own name -- libbotlish_boringssl.a -- so that no link ever takes
# another library named crypto or ssl (a system OpenSSL's) for it.
#
# The tag is an annotated tag object, not a signed one: its id and its
# commit are both pinned here, independently of the server that serves
# them, and the fetch checks both.
library boringssl
url https://boringssl.googlesource.com/boringssl
tag 0.20261020.0
tagObject 6b482f540b02a913d3dbec6fd5c4d598d523cf48
commit d3bf4795ad5b79d646cddf2fec687da5b9b502db
bindings {boring 5.4.0 boring-sys 5.4.0}
cmake {-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE=ON}
targets {crypto ssl}
